	"108": {
		"inputs": {
			"value": "Finish this partially inpainted image by seamlessly integrating the added object into the scene.\n\nThe inserted object must remain 100% identical to how it appears in the input — same shape, proportions, color, texture, material, pattern, and every visual detail. Treat the object's pixels as fixed content that must be preserved, not as a reference to reimagine.\n\nWHAT YOU SHOULD DO — ONLY SCENE INTEGRATION:\n- Blend the object's edges naturally into the background so the boundary is invisible.\n- Add physically accurate contact shadows and cast shadows consistent with the scene's existing light direction, intensity, and color temperature.\n- Add reflections or ambient occlusion only if the surface/environment would realistically produce them (e.g. glossy floor, glass, water).\n- Adjust only the object's overall brightness/color grading slightly if needed so it sits under the same lighting conditions as the rest of the scene — but never alter its actual hue, material, or design identity.\n- Match perspective, scale, and grounding (the object must sit correctly on/against the surface it touches, with a realistic contact point).\n\nREFERENCE IMAGE (if provided):\nIf a second image is given, use it strictly as a reference for the object's correct dimensions, proportions, and spatial placement within the scene. It is for measurement/positioning guidance only.\n\nOUTPUT:\nA single photorealistic image where the object looks like it was physically present in the scene when the photo was taken — untouched in identity, but fully harmonized in light, shadow, and perspective.\n\nAdditional instructions (if any):"
		},
		"class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
		"_meta": {
			"title": "System prompt"
		}
	},
